# Stencils and aspect ratios

A stencil marks the selected region and supplies its constraints. Put it inside the cropper as an ordinary child.

## Choose a shape

`RectangleStencil` supports free resizing, a fixed ratio, or a ratio range. `CircleStencil` supplies a square ratio and circular bounding-box option. Its circular display does not mask the exported bitmap; apply a mask separately if you need transparent corners.

<Example source={ChangingStencilExampleSource} title="ChangingStencilExample">
	<ChangingStencilExample />
</Example>

Conditional children let you switch shapes at runtime. One cropper may have at most one live registered stencil. If you provide children with no stencil, there is no implicit replacement. A cropper without children uses `RectangleStencil`.

## Set the ratio

Pass `aspectRatio={16 / 9}` to a rectangle, or use `minAspectRatio` and `maxAspectRatio` for a range:

```svelte
<Cropper {src}>
	<RectangleStencil minAspectRatio={1 / 2} maxAspectRatio={2} />
</Cropper>
```

You can also pass `aspectRatio={{ minimum: 1 / 2, maximum: 2 }}`. An explicit rectangle `aspectRatio` takes precedence over its convenience bounds. With the default constraint strategy, a cropper-level `aspectRatio` takes precedence over the stencil's suggested ratio; avoid conflicting values.

## Grid and controls

<Example source={StencilGridExampleSource} title="StencilGridExample">
	<StencilGridExample />
</Example>

`grid` enables the built-in grid during interactions. `movable={false}` stops stencil dragging; `resizable={false}` disables resizing. To hide controls too, pass `handlers={false}` and `lines={false}`. Both collections also accept direction maps: only entries set to `true` appear. Omitted collections use the stencil's defaults.

```svelte
<RectangleStencil
	aspectRatio={1}
	handlers={{ eastNorth: true, westSouth: true }}
	lines={false}
/>
```

`disabled` on the cropper disables its children as well. A child cannot override that with `disabled={false}`.

## Add content inside the selection

Both built-in stencils render their children inside the crop region. Add decorative guides there with `pointer-events: none` so the guides do not intercept drags. If you need different geometry or interactions, follow [Custom stencil](/docs/tutorials/custom-stencil) or [Print guides](/docs/tutorials/print-guides).

See [RectangleStencil](/docs/reference/rectangle-stencil), [CircleStencil](/docs/reference/circle-stencil), and [layout and lifecycle](/docs/guides/layout-and-lifecycle) for the full contracts.
